message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "System channel genesis block creation (U6) will be implemented as a separate public API function distinct from application channel genesis block creation to provide clear, purpose-built functionality for consumers.",
    "The existing CreateSignedConfigUpdateEnvelope function will be renamed to SignConfigUpdateEnvelope, and the SigningIdentity interface will be extended to include both SignConfigUpdate and SignConfigUpdateEnvelope methods to encapsulate all config update signing functionality in a single interface.",
    "All new config modification functions will reuse existing helper logic for group/org/policy operations used for other config groups to minimize code duplication and maintain consistency with existing package behavior.",
    "All new and updated functions will follow existing Hyperledger Fabric Go coding conventions, including consistent error handling, input validation, and naming patterns aligned with the rest of the configtx package.",
    "Example usage for all new functionality will be added to the existing example_test.go file in the configtx package, following the structure of existing examples to ensure consistency."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The supporting functions for retrieving dependent config fields referenced in U1 are already fully implemented, tested, and stable, so the full channel config retrieval function only needs to compose these existing utilities.",
    "Existing configtx package test infrastructure is sufficient to cover new functionality, with no need for major updates to test harnesses or mocking frameworks.",
    "The configtx package's existing internal representation of consortiums, orderer orgs, application orgs, and policies is consistent enough that new removal/update functions can reuse existing traversal and modification logic without requiring structural changes to the config model.",
    "No breaking changes to existing public APIs of the configtx package are required to implement the requested functionality, so existing consumer code will not be impacted by the changes.",
    "The GoDoc generation tooling for the project is already configured, so adding the Overview section to the configtx package will not require changes to documentation build pipelines."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement full channel config retrieval function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the public function to return a full config.Channel object by leveraging existing dependent field retrieval utilities, add input validation and error handling, and write unit tests for the new functionality to meet U1 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement channel creation policy update function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the function to update the default channel creation policy ConfigValue in the consortium group, add input validation, ensure integration with existing config update workflows, write unit tests, and add an example in example_test.go demonstrating usage to meet U2 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement channel group policy operations",
      "activity_description": "Develop three functions to add a policy to the channel group, remove a policy from the channel group, and retrieve all policies in the channel group, reuse existing policy helper logic for consistency, add input validation, write unit tests, and update existing examples to demonstrate the new operations to meet U3 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement organization removal from consortium, application, and orderer groups",
      "activity_description": "Develop three separate functions to remove an organization from a consortium, application group, and orderer group respectively, reuse existing org removal logic from other groups, add input validation, write unit tests, and update examples to show usage of each removal function to meet U4 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement consortium removal function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the function to remove a specified consortium from the channel config, add input validation to ensure proper cleanup of related references, write unit tests, and add an example in example_test.go demonstrating consortium removal to meet U5 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement system channel genesis block creation function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the public function to generate a system channel genesis block (with no application group, only orderer and consortiums groups in the channel config), add input validation, write unit tests, and add a new example in example_test.go demonstrating system channel genesis block creation to meet U6 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Add configtx package GoDoc overview",
      "activity_description": "Write a clear Overview section for the configtx package GoDoc explaining the package's purpose, usage, and channel structure, integrate it into the existing package documentation, and verify correct rendering in generated GoDocs to meet U7 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Extend SigningIdentity and rename config update signing function",
      "activity_description": "Extend the SigningIdentity interface to include SignConfigUpdate and SignConfigUpdateEnvelope (renamed from CreateSignedConfigUpdateEnvelope) methods, implement the methods, update all internal references and existing unit tests that use the old function name, add GoDoc documentation explaining the usage and differences between the two signing methods, and update existing examples that use the old function name to meet U8 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 70
  }
}

